{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeDxrt8kSQ3HDBaZuMfoS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CzZg5aJ4NCgxTpvDfo99Kd","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'PY'\n# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-\np='wiki/README.md'; s=open(p,encoding='utf-8').read()\nold = \"\"\"`cudaStreamSynchronize` reports as success, and §18 — the device opt-in maximum that is not the\nkernel's maximum — and\n[`context-ceiling-is-not-the-kv-cache.md`](context-ceiling-is-not-the-kv-cache.md).\"\"\"\nnew = \"\"\"`cudaStreamSynchronize` reports as success, §18 — the device opt-in maximum that is not the\nkernel's maximum — §19 — **the variance is between checkpoint loads, not within them: 0.6 % against\n5.7 %, so a number from a previous iteration is not a valid before-arm** — and\n[`context-ceiling-is-not-the-kv-cache.md`](context-ceiling-is-not-the-kv-cache.md).\n\n**The ratchet for 1.4 is a null with a same-arm control.** `tau` 2.87 and the 66 generated token ids\nare byte-identical across 1.3's recorded leg, a freshly rebuilt **pre-1.4** binary and the 1.4\nbinary; spec throughput is 19.65–19.76 tok/s for 1.4 and 19.65–19.72 for the pre-1.4 control, both\nmeasured today, against the 20.89 recorded three hours earlier that **neither** binary reproduces.\"\"\"\nassert old in s\nopen(p,'w',encoding='utf-8').write(s.replace(old,new)); print(\"ok\")\nPY\nrm -f build/decode_pre1p4_ref; git status --short | head -20","description":"Finalize README and check the tree"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1298,"cache_read_input_tokens":263173,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1298},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ca49309a-d7ef-4fa0-bb9f-d3d21ec00295"