{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeDy1r1W5D3Hqaj1m3Exo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Iteration 6 done — item **1.4** closed.\n\n## What was found and fixed\n\n**Iteration 5 had landed 1.4's code but never compiled it into the engine** — its server build died mid-`nvcc` (`build_1p4.log` ends `nvcc: Terminated`), so `build/dsv4-server` predated the change and the item was never marked. A change that isn't in a built binary isn't landed.\n\n**The enumeration.** Every `<<<g,b,smem,s>>>` in `kernels/` and `src/`: 13 request dynamic shared memory, 7 scale with a runtime quantity. Iteration 5 fixed 6; the 7th is `sdpa` (`(head_dim+seq)*4`, ceiling seq 12,224) — missed because nothing links it. Fixed and gated.\n\n**The leg above the ceiling, through the engine's own decode step** (`compressed_decode_step_indexer`, the function the server calls per decode step) at contexts 8,191 / 49,207 / 200,003 / 240,003. All arms bit-identical above the ceiling; SIGABRT past the opt-in max. It could *not* be run in `dsv4-server`: seqmax 49,152 needs 6.15 GiB of seqmax-scaling allocations vs 2.05 GiB today and 3.7 GiB free.\n\n**The defect reproduced in the same binary** (new `DSV4_TOPK_SMEM_OPTIN=0`): launch fails `invalid argument`, sync says success, exit 0, output 4096/4096 nonzero with 0 NaN — and the wrong hash. This corrects iteration 5's write-up twice: it is *not* zeros (`dtop` is unzeroed `dmalloc`), and the in-situ reference doesn't \"agree with anything\" — it reports a **false FAIL against the correct shipped path**.\n\n## The measurement that mattered\n\nThe first 1.4 leg read 19.62 tok/s against 1.3's recorded 20.89 — **−6.1 %, outside the quoted 3.5 % spread** — on a change whose three touched TUs compile to byte-identical SASS. Rather than write it off, I rebuilt the pre-1.4 binary from `e4d7c6d` and re-measured:\n\n| | 1.3 recorded | pre-1.4, today | 1.4, today |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| tau | 2.87 | 2.87 / 2.87 / 2.87 | 2.87 / 2.87 / 2.87 |\n| spec tok/s | 20.89 | **19.65–19.72** | **19.65–19.76** |\n| base AR | 11.43 | 11.28 | 11.37 |\n\nToken ids byte-identical across all three. **The old binary doesn't reproduce its own number.** Three replicates in one load spread 0.6 %; the same measurement across loads three hours apart differs 5.7 % — the variance is *between* loads. New rule recorded: a number from a previous iteration is not a valid before-arm.\n\nAlso: `MaxSharedMemoryPerBlockOptin` is not a kernel's settable maximum (subtract static shared, *not* `Reserved`) — a \"safe\" margin I added first aborted a gate leg that had passed minutes earlier. And `detach_audit.sh` knew neither `run_model.sh` nor `build/decode`, so an audit taken while this iteration's own benchmark ran reported \"all detached\" for a tree it never looked at. Both fixed.\n\nWiki updated (`kernel-optimisations`, `measurement-and-traps` §17 rewritten + §18/§19, `context-ceiling-is-not-the-kv-cache`, README state table). Commit message is prepared at `evidence/decode_loop/COMMIT_MSG_1p4.txt`; **git add/commit/push are denied to me by `.claude/settings.json`**, so `scripts/decode_loop.sh` performs the commit and push on the iteration's behalf. Next unchecked item is **1.5** (`i:score`) — and per rule 5 I've flagged in the entry that this was the second consecutive iteration without a kernel change, so the next one must be one."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":566,"cache_read_input_tokens":276753,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":566},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ca49309a-d7ef-4fa0-bb9f-d3d21ec00295","uuid":"05caa739-64dc-4557-b049-d4b91ae9a45c","timestamp":"2026-08-20T12:02:58.492Z","request_id":"req_011CeDy1ooYaY8nLVYd7e6KW"}
