{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeEWVcTKAGAEMzk1BKJbh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011tXiUYp1SjuWNvGQ9GPK6G","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > evidence/decode_loop/COMMIT_MSG_1p8.txt <<'EOF'\n1.8: the cattn:q_proj bimodality is the compressor emits on g_side, the \"free 4.4 ms\" does not exist, and the fork it exposed is worth a paired 0.81 ms/forward\n\nWHAT WAS ASKED. 0.4 left one open lead: at fixed verify width, fixed shape and fixed context,\n`q:wq_a` ran 1.71 ms on some verify steps and 5.47 on others -- a 3.2x swing in one fp8 GEMM, with\n`cattn:compress` splitting the same way. `cattn:q_proj` is 14.6 ms of every step, so 0.4 recorded\nthat \"if the cheap mode is reachable on demand that is ~4.4 ms/step of Term A for free\".\n\nWHAT IT IS. `compressed_verify_step_indexer` records `g_side_fork` and then issues `build_qKV` on\nthe MAIN stream, so the two `compressor_emit_group` calls run concurrently with the q chain\n(F55/F56). The emits fire only for groups completing inside the block -- `(j+1)%ratio==0` -- and the\ndprof marks are CUDA events on the main stream, so on an emit step they time a GEMM sharing the\nmemory system with 21 layers x 2 compressor emits, and on a non-emit step they time it alone.\n\nMEASURED, IN THREE INDEPENDENT WAYS.\n\n1. THE SCHEDULE, AT ZERO GPU COST. `g = #{ j in [ctx,ctx+VB) : (j+1)%4 == 0 }` comes straight out of\n   the dprof tag. It classifies 0.4's OWN 153 per-verify tables 153/153, gap 2.80x, no overlap\n   between the populations -- on data collected before the hypothesis existed. The excess is LINEAR\n   in g: q_proj+compress is +6.97 ms at g=1 and +14.78 at g=2.\n\n2. THE CAUSE, TWO ARMS, ONE BINARY, SERIAL FIRST SO DRIFT PENALISES THE SHIPPED ARM. Four\n   predictions registered in scripts/qproj_ab_run.sh before it ran; all four held. At VB=2 held\n   fixed (g correlates with width by construction):\n\n     arm     g   q:wq_a   cattn:q_proj   cattn:compress   sum\n     serial  0     1.65        10.11            0.05     10.16\n     serial  1     1.66        10.12            8.34     18.46\n     split   0     1.66        10.12            0.04     10.16\n     split   1     5.54        14.68            2.50     17.18\n\n   The swing exists only when the fork does: 1.00-1.02x serial, 3.05x split (174/174 separated).\n   The g=0 baseline is 10.16 ms in BOTH arms across two separate checkpoint loads.\n\n3. THE TAIL, UNPLANNED. Every cattn:compress sample above 20 ms -- 8 of 8 across both arms, 43-50 ms\n   each, plus the lone outlier in 0.4's table -- is a block containing a RATIO-128 boundary, i.e.\n   the 20 strided layers, which use no side stream at all.\n\nTHE RATCHET. Paired per leg, same corpus sha: 9 of 9 legs faster under the fork, mean -0.81\nms/forward, sd 0.14, 2 SE band [-0.90, -0.72]; 9/9 byte-identical, tau and realised width equal to\nthree decimals on every leg. The mark-level instrument predicts that band from the other side:\n1.29 ms hidden per emit step x 113/174 emit steps = 0.838 ms/forward, inside it.\n\nWHAT IT MEANS. There is no cheap mode; there is the absence of an emit. Overlap hides 16-17 % of the\ncompressor and the other 84 % is work a correct engine must do, so `a` stays 125.11 ms and 4.4 ms of\nphantom headroom leaves this ladder before an iteration was spent chasing it. What the item bought\ninstead is the first price on the compressed-KV emit: 7.02 ms on the 64.9 % of forwards that carry\none = 4.56 ms/forward amortised, 3.3 % of the forward, at 52 % of its 880 MB byte roofline.\n\nBIT-EXACTNESS. Nothing numeric changed in either arm -- NO_ATTN_SPLIT only moves kernels between\nstreams and the fork/join keeps the dependency order identical -- and 9/9 legs proved it.\n\nNEW ON THE LADDER, with pre-registered and honestly small ceilings: 1.11 defer the ATTN_SPLIT join\npast i:qidx/i:iw (1.99 ms of independent main-stream work is on the wrong side of it; ceiling\n1.29 ms/forward, and this item does NOT establish it is recoverable); 1.12 the ratio-128 emit\nre-reads its 33.55 MB of f32 weights ceil(256/8)=32 times (43-50 ms in a single step, ~0.53\nms/forward amortised).\n\nRULE 5 IS ONE ITERATION FROM FIRING. 1.7 shipped a kernel, 1.8 did not. The next iteration takes a\nkernel item.\n\nWIKI, same commit: measurement-and-traps.md §29 (a mark that timed another stream's work),\nnegative-results.md §4h (headroom that was never there), kernel-optimisations.md §2.4b (the\ncompressor fork, re-measured with a band), README.md state table gains an \"after 1.8\" column.\n\nInstruments: tools/qproj_bimodal.py (schedule classifier, runs on any dprof server log);\nscripts/qproj_ab_run.sh (both arms, detached, added to detach_audit.sh PATTERNS in this commit).\nEOF\ngit add -A && git commit -q -F evidence/decode_loop/COMMIT_MSG_1p8.txt && git log --oneline -1","description":"Commit iteration 6"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":207,"cache_read_input_tokens":173593,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":207},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"afb9b966-ee00-4592-a8ea-5fde6048a34a","uuid":"4f49111d-c3c5-4612-b7a2-fd38bbf51fab","timestamp":"2026-08-20T18:55:54.971Z","request_id":"req_011CeEWVbP5C2XuH6mf7DVVt"}
