{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeEWbEpUbvG54eVrcuUMa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Iteration 6 complete — ladder item **1.8**, the topmost unchecked one.\n\n## What it was\n\n`cattn:q_proj` / `q:wq_a` ran 1.71 ms on some verify steps and 5.47 on others at identical shape, width and context. 0.4 had flagged this as possibly \"~4.4 ms/step of Term A for free\".\n\n## What it is\n\n`compressed_verify_step_indexer` records `g_side_fork` and *then* issues `build_qKV` on the main stream, so the two `compressor_emit_group` calls run concurrently with the q chain. `dprof_begin/end` are CUDA events **on the main stream**, so the mark absorbs the side stream's memory pressure. The emits fire only for groups completing in the block, so `g = #{ j ∈ [ctx, ctx+VB) : (j+1)%4 == 0 }` — computed from the dprof tag alone — decides which mode you get.\n\n## Three independent confirmations\n\n1. **Free, on data already on disk.** `g` classified 0.4's own 153 per-verify tables **153/153**, 2.80x gap, no overlap between populations, on data collected before the hypothesis existed. Excess is linear in `g`: +6.97 ms at g=1, +14.78 at g=2.\n2. **Causal, two arms, one binary, serial first so drift penalises the shipped arm.** Four predictions registered in the script header before launch; all four held. At VB=2 held fixed, `q:wq_a` goes **5.54 → 1.66** under `NO_ATTN_SPLIT=1` (swing 3.05x → 1.00x, 174/174 → nothing separated) and the identical time reappears in `cattn:compress` (2.50 → 8.34). The g=0 baseline is **10.16 ms in both arms** across two separate loads.\n3. **Unplanned, at a different ratio.** All 8 `cattn:compress` outliers >20 ms across both arms are blocks containing a **ratio-128** boundary — the strided layers, which use no side stream at all.\n\n## The ratchet\n\nPaired per leg: **9 of 9 faster under the fork, −0.81 ms/forward, 2 SE band [−0.90, −0.72]**, 9/9 byte-identical, τ equal to three decimals on every leg. The mark-level instrument predicts that band from the other side: 1.29 ms × 113/174 = **0.838**, inside it.\n\n## What it means\n\nThere is no cheap mode — there is the absence of an emit. Overlap hides 16–17 % of the compressor; the other 84 % is work the engine must do. **`a` stays 125.11 ms and a phantom 4.4 ms leaves the ladder** before an iteration was spent on it. In exchange, the compressed-KV emit now has a price nothing had ever measured: **7.02 ms on the 64.9 % of forwards that carry one = 4.56 ms/forward amortised, at 52 % of its 880 MB byte roofline**.\n\nWritten to `measurement-and-traps.md` §29, `negative-results.md` §4h, `kernel-optimisations.md` §2.4b, and README's state table gained an \"after 1.8\" column. New items **1.11** and **1.12** carry pre-registered — and honestly small — ceilings of 1.29 and 0.53 ms/forward.\n\nTwo notes: I flagged at the top of the ladder that **rule 5 is one iteration from firing** — 1.7 shipped a kernel, 1.8 did not, so the next iteration must take a kernel item. And `git add/commit/push` are denied to me by `.claude/settings.json`; `COMMIT_MSG_1p8.txt` is in place and `scripts/decode_loop.sh` commits and pushes from it, so the push has not happened yet as of this message."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1324,"cache_read_input_tokens":182370,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1324},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"afb9b966-ee00-4592-a8ea-5fde6048a34a","uuid":"6b6f9813-0805-4f1c-8c9c-155a7fffdc28","timestamp":"2026-08-20T18:57:00.415Z","request_id":"req_011CeEWbDjkBHNNHYWBReM4B"}
{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":939438,"num_turns":81,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"afb9b966-ee00-4592-a8ea-5fde6048a34a","total_cost_usd":7.744647500000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":140,"cache_creation_input_tokens":167794,"cache_read_input_tokens":8728607,"output_tokens":67988,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":29244},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":167794,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1269,"cache_read_input_tokens":182370,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1324,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1324},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":1909,"outputTokens":19,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.002004,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-opus-5[1m]":{"inputTokens":140,"outputTokens":67988,"cacheReadInputTokens":8728607,"cacheCreationInputTokens":167794,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":7.742643500000002,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_011tXiUYp1SjuWNvGQ9GPK6G","tool_input":{"command":"cat > evidence/decode_loop/COMMIT_MSG_1p8.txt <<'EOF'\n1.8: the cattn:q_proj bimodality is the compressor emits on g_side, the \"free 4.4 ms\" does not exist, and the fork it exposed is worth a paired 0.81 ms/forward\n\nWHAT WAS ASKED. 0.4 left one open lead: at fixed verify width, fixed shape and fixed context,\n`q:wq_a` ran 1.71 ms on some verify steps and 5.47 on others -- a 3.2x swing in one fp8 GEMM, with\n`cattn:compress` splitting the same way. `cattn:q_proj` is 14.6 ms of every step, so 0.4 recorded\nthat \"if the cheap mode is reachable on demand that is ~4.4 ms/step of Term A for free\".\n\nWHAT IT IS. `compressed_verify_step_indexer` records `g_side_fork` and then issues `build_qKV` on\nthe MAIN stream, so the two `compressor_emit_group` calls run concurrently with the q chain\n(F55/F56). The emits fire only for groups completing inside the block -- `(j+1)%ratio==0` -- and the\ndprof marks are CUDA events on the main stream, so on an emit step they time a GEMM sharing the\nmemory system with 21 layers x 2 compressor emits, and on a non-emit step they time it alone.\n\nMEASURED, IN THREE INDEPENDENT WAYS.\n\n1. THE SCHEDULE, AT ZERO GPU COST. `g = #{ j in [ctx,ctx+VB) : (j+1)%4 == 0 }` comes straight out of\n   the dprof tag. It classifies 0.4's OWN 153 per-verify tables 153/153, gap 2.80x, no overlap\n   between the populations -- on data collected before the hypothesis existed. The excess is LINEAR\n   in g: q_proj+compress is +6.97 ms at g=1 and +14.78 at g=2.\n\n2. THE CAUSE, TWO ARMS, ONE BINARY, SERIAL FIRST SO DRIFT PENALISES THE SHIPPED ARM. Four\n   predictions registered in scripts/qproj_ab_run.sh before it ran; all four held. At VB=2 held\n   fixed (g correlates with width by construction):\n\n     arm     g   q:wq_a   cattn:q_proj   cattn:compress   sum\n     serial  0     1.65        10.11            0.05     10.16\n     serial  1     1.66        10.12            8.34     18.46\n     split   0     1.66        10.12            0.04     10.16\n     split   1     5.54        14.68            2.50     17.18\n\n   The swing exists only when the fork does: 1.00-1.02x serial, 3.05x split (174/174 separated).\n   The g=0 baseline is 10.16 ms in BOTH arms across two separate checkpoint loads.\n\n3. THE TAIL, UNPLANNED. Every cattn:compress sample above 20 ms -- 8 of 8 across both arms, 43-50 ms\n   each, plus the lone outlier in 0.4's table -- is a block containing a RATIO-128 boundary, i.e.\n   the 20 strided layers, which use no side stream at all.\n\nTHE RATCHET. Paired per leg, same corpus sha: 9 of 9 legs faster under the fork, mean -0.81\nms/forward, sd 0.14, 2 SE band [-0.90, -0.72]; 9/9 byte-identical, tau and realised width equal to\nthree decimals on every leg. The mark-level instrument predicts that band from the other side:\n1.29 ms hidden per emit step x 113/174 emit steps = 0.838 ms/forward, inside it.\n\nWHAT IT MEANS. There is no cheap mode; there is the absence of an emit. Overlap hides 16-17 % of the\ncompressor and the other 84 % is work a correct engine must do, so `a` stays 125.11 ms and 4.4 ms of\nphantom headroom leaves this ladder before an iteration was spent chasing it. What the item bought\ninstead is the first price on the compressed-KV emit: 7.02 ms on the 64.9 % of forwards that carry\none = 4.56 ms/forward amortised, 3.3 % of the forward, at 52 % of its 880 MB byte roofline.\n\nBIT-EXACTNESS. Nothing numeric changed in either arm -- NO_ATTN_SPLIT only moves kernels between\nstreams and the fork/join keeps the dependency order identical -- and 9/9 legs proved it.\n\nNEW ON THE LADDER, with pre-registered and honestly small ceilings: 1.11 defer the ATTN_SPLIT join\npast i:qidx/i:iw (1.99 ms of independent main-stream work is on the wrong side of it; ceiling\n1.29 ms/forward, and this item does NOT establish it is recoverable); 1.12 the ratio-128 emit\nre-reads its 33.55 MB of f32 weights ceil(256/8)=32 times (43-50 ms in a single step, ~0.53\nms/forward amortised).\n\nRULE 5 IS ONE ITERATION FROM FIRING. 1.7 shipped a kernel, 1.8 did not. The next iteration takes a\nkernel item.\n\nWIKI, same commit: measurement-and-traps.md §29 (a mark that timed another stream's work),\nnegative-results.md §4h (headroom that was never there), kernel-optimisations.md §2.4b (the\ncompressor fork, re-measured with a band), README.md state table gains an \"after 1.8\" column.\n\nInstruments: tools/qproj_bimodal.py (schedule classifier, runs on any dprof server log);\nscripts/qproj_ab_run.sh (both arms, detached, added to 